# Anything the Linux CI runner executes must stay LF, whatever a Windows editor
# or core.autocrlf does to the working copy. A `run:` block checked out with CRLF
# hands bash a trailing \r on every line — `case` patterns stop matching and the
# failure reads as a logic bug, not a line-ending one.
/.github/**  text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.mjs        text eol=lf

# Scoped deliberately. A repo-wide `* text=auto` would renormalize every tracked
# file in one commit and bury the next real diff.
